/* ============================================================================
   exponential-equation.epher -- solve 2^x = 12 via logarithms

   Take natural logarithms of both sides: x ln 2 = ln 12, so x = ln(12)/ln(2)
   (any algebra text, e.g. Stewart, Redlin and Watson, "College Algebra",
   7th ed., sec. 5.5). The value is irrational, so it prints to about 12
   significant digits; raising 2 back to that power returns 12 within
   rounding, which the last line checks to 1e-9. The built-in solve could
   scan the equation numerically too; the logarithm rearrangement is the
   classic method and is exact up to the final rounding.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/algebra/equations/exponential-equation.epher"

   The knob to edit is rhs below.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knob ----------------------------------------------------------------
const rhs = 12                             // solve 2^x = rhs

// ---- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------
def lnx(rhs) = ln(rhs) / ln(2)             // x from x ln 2 = ln rhs

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
print("x:", lnx(rhs))
print("2^x:", 2 ^ lnx(rhs))
print("2^x = 12 within 1e-9:", abs(2 ^ lnx(rhs) - rhs) < 1e-9)
/* ---- expected output ----
= 12
= x: 3.58496250072
= 2^x: 12
= 2^x = 12 within 1e-9: true
*/
